    "content": "Billy Bush (William Hall Bush) is an American radio and television host, best known as a former correspondent and anchor for Access Hollywood (2001–2016) and a former co-host of NBC’s Today show. He is a member of the Bush political family, being the nephew of President George H.W. Bush and cousin to President George W. Bush. Key Details About Billy Bush: Access Hollywood & Controversy: He was the primary anchor for Access Hollywood and later joined Today. In 2016, he was fired from Today following the release of a 2005 Access Hollywood tape where he was heard engaging in lewd conversation with Donald Trump. Family Background: Born to Josephine Colwell Bush and banker Jonathan Bush, he is part of the prominent political family. Career Highlights: Before Access Hollywood, he hosted Billy Bush and The Bush League Morning Show on WWZZ-FM in Washington, D.C.. He also hosted the Miss Universe pageant and served as a correspondent for multiple Olympics. Return to Media: After the 2016 tape scandal, Bush returned to television as the host of Extra in 2019. Note: There have been recent interviews in 2025/2026 where Bush has reflected on his career and the 2005 tape scandal.",
